Patch Set 2:

Michael, there is one question left, which stops me from propagating errors to onError() callback of Observable

These is possible situation, when we might retrieve errors mixed with results. AFAIR it still probable, because of distributed view queries. And they looks like this:

 {
   "total_rows": 3,
   "rows": [ {...}, {...}, {...} ],
   "errors": [
     {
       "from": "127.0.0.1:5984",
       "reason": "Design document `_design/testfoobar` missing in database `test_db_b`."
     },
     {
       "from": "http:// localhost:5984/_view_merge/",
       "reason": "Design document `_design/testfoobar` missing in database `test_db_c`."
     }
   ]
 }

At this moment I don't see how I can call onError() except to raise exception, but in this case I will not be able to return result object with partial result.

Does it seem like enough for leaving it as is? Probably we should also document, why some errors returned in the result object? (becase there is some other useful information in this object)

Patch Set 3:

Netty will report it heuristically, but you can increase the verbosity and likelyhood through:

    static {
            ResourceLeakDetector.setLevel(ResourceLeakDetector.Level.ADVANCED);
    }

Patch Set 5: Code-Review+1 Verified+1

@intae I added tests, made a few corrections (javadoc and method naming) and run the full integration+unit test suite, this is now Verified+1.

@michael can you CodeReview+2 before this can be submitted?

Patch Set 1:

discussed with mark in gitter, the arrayAppendAll prefix seems like a good solution

we could add support for both varargs and collections in this case

choice would be between the following three signature sets:

either (consistent with simple arrayAppend, but varargs is constrained to have different param order)

arrayAppendAll(String path, Collection<T> values, boolean createParents);
arrayAppendAll(String path, boolean createParents, T... values);

or (consistent with other signatures, varargs forfeits the ability to set createParents)

arrayAppendAll(String path, Collection<T> values, boolean createParents);
arrayAppendAll(String path, T... values); //defaults to createParents = false

or (consistency between the too "xxxAll" method but not with the rest of the specs)

arrayAppendAll(String path, boolean createParent, Collection<T> values);
arrayAppendAll(String path, boolean createParents, T... values);
